      {
        "id": "p72-q10-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Rewrite in the form $k_1P(C-P)$ or $k_2P\\left(1-\\frac{P}{C}\\right)$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=\\dfrac{3}{8000}P(160\\,000-P)$ or $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=60P\\left(1-\\dfrac{P}{160\\,000}\\right)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{dP}{dt}&=3P\\left(\\frac{160\\,000-P}{8000}\\right)\\\\\\frac{dP}{dt}&=\\frac{3}{8000}P(160\\,000-P)\\\\\\frac{dP}{dt}&=60P\\left(1-\\frac{P}{160\\,000}\\right).\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 23
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q10-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence identify the carrying capacity.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$160\\,000$ cockroaches.",
          "worked": "Comparing with $\\dfrac{dP}{dt}=k_1P(C-P)$ gives $C=160\\,000$. The carrying capacity is $160\\,000$ cockroaches.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p72-q10-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": {
          "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
          "version": 1,
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "p72-q10-c-instruction",
              "type": "paragraph",
              "fontSize": null,
              "align": "left",
              "spaceBefore": 0,
              "spaceAfter": 2,
              "lineHeight": 1.4,
              "indent": 0,
              "inlines": [
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "By using the equation of ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "math",
                  "latex": "\\frac{dP}{dt}",
                  "display": false
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": " and ",
                  "marks": []
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": "no calculus",
                  "marks": [
                    "bold"
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "type": "text",
                  "text": ", explain why the rate of increase is greatest at half the carrying capacity.",
                  "marks": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "The rate is a downward-opening quadratic in $P$, with zeros at $0$ and $160\\,000$. Its maximum is midway between them, at $P=80\\,000$ cockroaches.",
          "worked": "The rate of increase is\n$$\\frac{dP}{dt}=\\frac{3}{8000}P(160\\,000-P).$$\nAs a function of $P$, this is a downward-opening parabola with roots $P=0$ and $P=160\\,000$. These are the populations at which the rate of change is zero. By symmetry, its maximum occurs halfway between the roots:\n$$P=\\frac{0+160\\,000}{2}=80\\,000.$$\nThus the rate of increase is greatest at half the carrying capacity.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 29
      }
    ]
